module

-- This file is hand-written. A signature install leaves it alone, so what is
-- put here is kept.
--
-- It is a stub: what stands here is a description of what belongs in it.
--
-- The soundness theorem, stated about the text of a proof file: if the checker
-- prints `correct` for this input, the assumptions the parser read out of it are
-- unsatisfiable.
--
-- This is the top of the development. It is deliberately kept out of the library
-- root, because it depends on the whole rule-correctness tree and so on every
-- proof under `Proofs/Rules/`, which is far too expensive to build as part of the
-- default target.
--
-- In Logos: `Cpc/ApiCorrect.lean`, whose `correct___logos_check_proof` this
-- corresponds to.

public import @CALCULUS@.ApiChecks
import all @CALCULUS@.ApiChecks
public import @CALCULUS@.Proofs.Checker
import all @CALCULUS@.Proofs.Checker

public section
